{"type":"META","ticket":300,"id":"META"}||{"title":"LCSC_CAP1296-1-AIA-TR","tags":[],"source":"","images":[],"attributes":{"Symbol":"736c256724265401","Footprint":"","Description":"Six-channel capacitive touch controller; I2C 0x28; DFN-10 + exposed GND","Name":"LCSC_CAP1296-1-AIA-TR","Designator":"U?","Value":"CAP1296-1-AIA-TR","LCSC_Candidate_Unverified":"C2652051","Footprint_Candidate_Status":"custom_datasheet_land_candidate_not_board_validated","Design_Notes":"CAP1296-1-AIA-TR; 3.3V supply; fixed 7-bit I2C 0x28. DFN10 exposed ground pad is numbered 11 in this custom symbol and footprint. All six CS inputs wired through 1k resistors to ELE0..ELE5. CS3/SG used as CS3, no guard. R6=10k IRQ pull-up; C11=100nF/C12=1uF supply bypass. Enable only physically fitted electrodes in firmware; disable and ground unused CS inputs per datasheet. Tune thresholds and filtering on actual enclosure. Measure I2C rise time with final bus capacitance and existing pull-ups. GPIO40 IRQ is preserved and is not RTC deep-sleep wake. Firmware critical: clear 0x2A MULT_BLK_EN bit7 for simultaneous grip/rim touches; keep MTP_EN disabled and 0x20 MAX_DUR_EN bit3=0 for long grip. Any unused CS channel must be disabled and grounded, not left floating. Engineering candidate, not tested hardware.","UserDocLink":"https://ww1.microchip.com/downloads/en/DeviceDoc/00001569B.pdf","ReviewStatus":"datasheet_pin_package_checked_engineering_candidate","Comment":"CAP1296-1-AIA-TR","MPN":"CAP1296-1-AIA-TR","Manufacturer":"Microchip Technology","LCSC":"C2652051","JLCPCB Part #":"C2652051","Catalog_Status":"official_in_production; catalog_directory_identity_verified; engineering_candidate","Catalog_URL":"https://www.lcsc.com/product-detail/C2652051.html","Selection_Blocker":"Hardware bring-up, touch/EMC/ESD tuning and PCB footprint/stencil review remain open.","Catalog_Notes":"CAP1296-1-AIA-TR; 3.3V supply; fixed 7-bit I2C 0x28. DFN10 exposed ground pad is numbered 11 in this custom symbol and footprint. All six CS inputs wired through 1k resistors to ELE0..ELE5. CS3/SG used as CS3, no guard. R6=10k IRQ pull-up; C11=100nF/C12=1uF supply bypass. Enable only physically fitted electrodes in firmware; disable and ground unused CS inputs per datasheet. Tune thresholds and filtering on actual enclosure. Measure I2C rise time with final bus capacitance and existing pull-ups. GPIO40 IRQ is preserved and is not RTC deep-sleep wake. Firmware critical: clear 0x2A MULT_BLK_EN bit7 for simultaneous grip/rim touches; keep MTP_EN disabled and 0x20 MAX_DUR_EN bit3=0 for long grip. Any unused CS channel must be disabled and grounded, not left floating. Engineering candidate, not tested hardware.","Candidate_Disclaimer":"工程候选：未完成硬件测试、PCB/钢网复核与采购放行。","Add into BOM":"yes","Origin Footprint":"Spirit_Touch:CAP1296_DFN-10-1EP_3x3mm_P0.5mm_EP1.6x2.3mm"}}|
